  nodeTextLayers:
  - Multiple G Proteins can come by and couple with an activated GLP1-R.
  - The G Protein is composed of three smaller subunits- alpha, beta, and gamma.
  - While G Protein is coupled with GLP1-R, its alpha subunit becomes activated,
    causing it to split off.
  - G-alpha and G-beta-gamma can rejoin as G Protein once again after  G-alpha gets
    deactivated.
